  "english": "23. Sunday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. Second [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 2 [badz, բձ]: \"To the Tomb\" (I gerezman) and \"They Came to the Tomb\" (Yekin i gerezman). Eve of the Fast of the Cross of Varag.\n24. Monday. Tone 2 [bekg, ԲԿ]. Fast. Saint Mamas, etc. Fathers Hymn Tone 8 [dadz, դձ]: \"We Who Hope\" (Yousatsyalqn).\n26. Wednesday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳԿ]. Fast. Fathers Hymn Tone 5 [gadz, գձ]: \"Glorified Is Your Name Forever\" (Paravoryal anoun ko yavedyan), O Lord God.\n30. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahg, ԱԿ]. Third [Sunday of Cross]. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The meat-eating period is seven weeks.\nOctober:\n7. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahf, ԱՁ]. Fourth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 1 [ahf, ած]: \"Glory to the Resurrection\" (Parg haroutyan) and \"Along with\" (Und ka).\n14. Sunday. Tone 4 [dadg, ԴԿ]. Fifth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 4 [dadg, դկ]: \"When They Came\" (Yorzham yekin) and \"The Angel Descended\" (Ej hreshtakn) and \"The Choir of Angels\" (Hreshtakatsn dasq).\n21. Sunday. Tone 4 [dadz, ԴԶ / ԴՁ]. Sixth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 4 [dadz, դձ]: \"To the Women\" (Kanantsn) and \"With an Awesome Voice\" (Ahagin dzayniv).\n28. Sunday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳԿ]. Seventh [Sunday of Cross]. Discovery of the Holy Cross.\n30. Tuesday. Tone 4 [dadg, ԴԿ]. Saints Hyperichius and Severian, etc. Fathers Hymn Tone 5 [gadz, գձ]: \"You Who the Torments of the Lawless\" (Ork ztanjans anorinats).\n31. Wednesday. Tone 1 [ahf, ԱՁ]. Fathers Hymn Tone 5 [gadz, գձ]: \"Blessed Are You, O Lord\" (Orhnyal es ter). For the Covenant. And see the rest according to the order.\nNovember:\n3. Saturday. Tone 2 [bekg, ԲԿ]. All Saints, old and new, etc.\n4. Sunday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳՁ]. Eighth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 3 [gadz, գձ]: \"By the Sign of the Cross\" (Aykhachanishn / I khachanishn).\n11. Sunday. Tone 2 [bekg, ԲԿ]. Ninth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 2 [bekg, բկ]: \"Christ Is Risen\" (Kristos haryav) to the end.\n18. Sunday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. Tenth [Sunday of Cross]. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 2 [badz, բձ]: \"That Evangelizing Voice\" (Zayn avedavor) to the end. Eve of the Fast of the Fifty Days [Advent].\n19. Monday. Tone 2 [bekg, ԲԿ]. Fast of the Fifty Days [Advent]. Fathers Hymn Tone 5 [gadz, գձ]: \"God of Our Fathers Who Saved\" (Hartsn merots astuats or prgetser).\n21. Wednesday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳԿ]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n25. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahg, ԱԿ]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Hymn Tone 2 [badz, բձ]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anabagan). Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 1 [ahg, ակ]: \"Risen\" (Haroubyal) and \"The Wonderful Angel\" (Sqancheli hreshtakn).\n26. Monday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. Saints Julian and Vasilouhi. Fathers Hymn Tone 1 [ahg, ակ]: \"Holy God, Creator\" (Sourb astuats ararich).\nDecember:\n2. Sunday. Tone 1 [ahf, ԱՁ]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Hymn Tone 2 [bekg, բկ]: \"Without Beginning, God\" (Ansgizbn astuats). Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 1 [ahf, ած]: \"Who by Ineffable Essence\" (Or anchar eutyamp).\n3. Monday. Tone 1 [ahg, ԱԿ]. Saints Gennarius and Mercurius, and James and Rhypasimus [Iravapar].\n4. Tuesday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. King Abgar. Lectionary Readings and Gospel of Theodosius.\n9. Sunday. Tone 4 [dadg, ԴԿ]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n12. Wednesday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. Fathers Hymn Tone 4 [dadz, դձ]: \"Lord God of\" (Ter astuats mer).\n16. Sunday. Tone 4 [dadz, ԴՁ]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Hymn Tone 5 [gadz, գձ]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paravoryal ordi). Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 4 [dadz, դձ]: \"You Who Are Above\" (Or i ver es).\n22. Saturday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳՁ]. Holy Patriarchs Basil, etc.\n23. Sunday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳԿ]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Fathers Hymn Tone 3 [gadz, գկ]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhayavedyan). Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 3 [gadz, գկ]: \"Your Resurrection\" (Zko yaroutyund) and \"Taking\" (Aryal).\n24. Monday. Tone 4 [dadz, ԴՁ]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n29. Saturday. Tone 2 [bekg, ԲԿ]. Sons of Thunder [Saints James and John]. Eve of the Nativity Fast.\n30. Sunday. Tone 3 [gadz, ԳՁ]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Resurrection Night Office Hymn Tone 3 [gadz, գձ]: \"Glorified Is Your\" (Paravoryal e ko) to the end.\n31. Monday. Tone 4 [dadg, ԴԿ]. Fast. Fathers Hymn of Fasting Tone 4 [dadg, դկ]: \"Blessed Are You, Lord God of Our Fathers\" (Orhnyal ter astuats hartsn merots), and so forth in order.\nJanuary:\n5. Saturday. Tone 2 [badz, ԲՁ]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ [Theophany].",
